/*!
    \page qtprofiler-getting-started.html
    \previouspage index.html
    \nextpage qtprofiler-how-to-record-a-trace.html

    \title Getting started

    To record and analyze profiling data:

    \list
        \li Start \QP from \QC or \QVSC, or install it as a stand-alone tool
            on Linux, \macos, or Windows.
        \li Select \uicontrol {Start recording}.
        \li Use the application to collect data.
        \li Select \uicontrol {Stop recording} to view the results.
        \li Inspect the results in the \QP views.
    \endlist

    \section1 Supported trace formats

    You can record and import trace files in the following formats:

    \list
        \li QML traces (\c {*.qtd}, \c {*.qzt})
        \li Chrome Trace Format (\c {*.json})
        \li Common Trace Format
    \endlist

    \section1 Supported analyzers

    You can use the following tools:

    \list
        \li QML Profiler
        \li Perf
        \li Chrome Trace Format (CTF) visualizer
    \endlist

    \sa {Record a trace}, {Command-line options}
*/
